1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,894
Everyone knows the eighty-twenty rule,

2
00:00:02,894 --> 00:00:05,255
yet almost nobody runs the math

3
00:00:05,255 --> 00:00:06,321
a second time.

4
00:00:06,321 --> 00:00:07,235
When you do,

5
00:00:07,235 --> 00:00:09,520
a hidden second layer appears.

6
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:10,119
In 1896,

7
00:00:10,119 --> 00:00:13,487
Italian economist Vilfredo Pareto showed that

8
00:00:13,487 --> 00:00:16,031
about twenty percent of the people

9
00:00:16,031 --> 00:00:18,651
in Italy owned about eighty percent

10
00:00:18,651 --> 00:00:19,549
of the land.

11
00:00:19,549 --> 00:00:21,944
The popular story about pea pods

12
00:00:21,944 --> 00:00:23,890
in his garden is a legend.

13
00:00:23,890 --> 00:00:26,597
Marketing writer Perry Marshall points out

14
00:00:26,597 --> 00:00:28,273
that if the pattern holds,

15
00:00:28,273 --> 00:00:30,142
Pareto repeats inside itself.

16
00:00:30,142 --> 00:00:32,527
Take twenty percent of twenty percent

17
00:00:32,527 --> 00:00:34,912
and eighty percent of eighty percent:

18
00:00:34,912 --> 00:00:37,039
just four percent of your actions

19
00:00:37,039 --> 00:00:39,810
could create sixty-four percent of results.

20
00:00:39,810 --> 00:00:41,791
Run it one layer deeper and

21
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:43,918
less than one percent of your

22
00:00:43,918 --> 00:00:46,338
choices could drive about half of

23
00:00:46,338 --> 00:00:47,292
your results.

24
00:00:47,292 --> 00:00:50,373
Busy people polish the ninety-six percent;

25
00:00:50,373 --> 00:00:52,060
builders guard the one.

26
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:53,010
Every Monday,

27
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:55,934
look at twenty-five things competing for

28
00:00:55,934 --> 00:00:56,665
your week,

29
00:00:56,665 --> 00:00:58,053
circle the top one,

30
00:00:58,053 --> 00:01:01,050
and finish it before touching your inbox.
